{"name":"Havasu","hex":"#007993","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Havasupai","blocks":[{"text":"The Havasupai people are a Native American people and tribe who have lived in the Grand Canyon for at least the past 800 years. Their name means \"people of the blue-green water\", referring to Havasu Creek, a tributary of the Colorado."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Havasupai_woman.jpg/330px-Havasupai_woman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havasupai","wikidata":"Q1500686"},{"title":"Havasu Creek","blocks":[{"text":"Havasu Creek is a stream in the U.S. state of Arizona. It is a tributary to the Colorado River, which it joins in the Grand Canyon. It primarily runs through the Havasupai Indian Reservation. It is sometimes called Cataract Creek, and should not be confused with Cataract Canyon, Utah."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/National_Park_Service_%2848754079298%29.jpg/330px-National_Park_Service_%2848754079298%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havasu_Creek","wikidata":"Q5683163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg/500px-Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg/1280px-Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg/500px-Havasupai_Basket_1907%2C_GCNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Havasupai Basket, c. 1907","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHavasupai_Basket_1